      GUI comments
      ------------

The GUI is just a frontend for the program, only for single runs.  It
uses expect, which is fairly standard on Linux, but also available on
other machines.  It makes life simple, but isn't really needed to run
the program. It provides defaults, which can be customized.  After GO
has been pressed for the first time, the molecule can't be changed any
more, if you want to do this, use Exit and start again.

The GUI allows for a personal initialisation file for all the
variables, ~/.lvg .  In there, the following variables can be
customized:

# program - HAS to be customized to the local installation
set lvg_prog /home/schilke/transfer/lvg/generic/lvg

# initialisation - just for site initialisation
# for private initialisation, use ~/.lvg

set molecule co
set n_levels 10
# now parameters
set temperature 10
set n_H2 1e4
set n_e 0
set n_mol 1e15
set t_d $temperature
set N_H2 0
set vgrad 1
set t_back 100
set beta_back 2
set tau100mic 1
set w_back 0
set te 10000
set em 1e9
set w_hii 0

set font 		-Adobe-Helvetica-Medium-R-Normal--14-140-*-*-*-*-*-*
set prompt_font		-Adobe-Helvetica-Bold-R-Normal--14-140-*-*-*-*-*-*



Peter Schilke <schilke@mpifr-bonn.mpg.de>
